  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_e7e951bc42f04b2481614932a2970138",
      "statement": "The RPO=0 and single-writer promises depend on the object store providing conditional create, conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency; Amazon S3, R2, Tigris, GCS, and Azure qualify, and celld is explicitly incorrect on stores without working conditional writes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L17-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eab3b00be254567d0b16e3622969d363a066b0474b8a028324efa4b26b264d00:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5fd5e5ade4ab4a389afa84ab7cbe1357",
      "statement": "The output gate holds every egress that can reveal cell state until its writes are proven durable: the shell sends Event::Output with the committed WAL position, State::output stores the Channel without branching on it, a write opens its own barrier with AwaitDurable, and a read-only output trails the newest open barrier on its cell or releases immediately if none is open.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L5-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4188d2499e1b70a8046ceec398e39ee51f78ed020028fe1364877151fc4aa940:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L68-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c7073b9403e61aefb98cad0417dc829b285763184dbdffeba5d779d42b51257:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c948740421a348d990a48579d9047ae4",
      "statement": "Alarm commits open barriers in the same per-cell map so readers trail an unproven alarm write, and a streaming response body is gated once at release rather than per chunk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L42-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ccf57ea8b00a0921cdbb7ae991734fec8af043420b444cf701054b061a8fb981:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1e31fff8f8d4d9b859bbf33d0cf7970",
      "statement": "durable_reached acknowledges only when the proved position covers the gated write; a bucket proof must additionally pass a VerifyOwnership read proving own.json still names this node at this epoch, while a fleet proof settles without that read because takeover sealing of followers arbitrates it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L167-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42681acc77860cbbc5e6e7d9efecfcdf36e532d4a04c98b0733e28f11be98e09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_db953165d0ab4136a1d98d35592f236a",
      "statement": "An unproven or ownership-failed gate releases with DurabilityUnproven and resets the cell (StopCause::Reset: stop the runtime, keep no local snapshot, restore from the bucket), because after refusing the write, serving its local state would be divergence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/output_gate.rs#L232-L284",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:101327e127ee63278946c3aec3c4d2403dc22c516cb4a902dda946a199037591:"
