    {
      "id": "claim_c0f8cb29c5a442e7aca55d449ff67b8d",
      "statement": "Slow followers are evicted by a pure windowed rule (append-latency tail above max(absolute budget, k times the sibling median), or a hard outstanding backstop) with reconfigurations rate-capped rather than the member excluded, and the leader hedges a slow append adaptively (default 4x the slowest recent append, floored at 250 ms) because appends are idempotent per sequence.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/log_evict.rs#L3-L12",
