    {
      "id": "claim_be41d88e28ce4d49ba43203615310c17",
      "statement": "A restore selects the newest nonempty epoch prefix under cells/<cell>/ltx/ and replays the full contiguous chain from transaction zero, because a recovery or bundle drain can append an acknowledged tail after an earlier restore; celld no longer writes epoch seal objects and legacy seals do not limit the chain.",
      "evidence": [
